    <label>Sassanid Empire</label>
    <description>The Empire of the Iranians, Eranshahr, ruled from Ctesiphon by the Sassanid King of Kings, heir of Cyrus and Darius and Rome's equal and rival for two hundred years. Its heart is the savaran, the armoured noble cavalry: clibanarii hidden in iron and mail, lancers and mace-bearers who can break any line, and horse archers who can destroy it from afar. Behind them stand spara archers and paighan levies, Dailamite hillmen with axes, Arab camel riders and the dreaded war elephants. They worship Ahura Mazda in the sacred fire, and they are at war with both Roman empires and with the Huns who raid their northern frontier.</description>
